  "story": {
    "headline": "A Simple Change to Sleep Directly Boosts Academic Performance, Study Reveals",
    "summary": "Sleep is the panacea of our time. A vast and growing body of research shows that when we get good sleep, good things happen inside our bodies.",
    "publisher": "Rally News",
    "url": "https://rally.news/categories/ai/?article=A%2BSimple%2BChange%2Bto%2BSleep%2BDirectly%2BBoosts%2BAcademic%2BPerformance%2C%2BStudy%2BReveals"
  },
  "researchBrief": "The study, published in the Journal of Political Economy, involved over 1,100 university students in the U.S. and found that incentives for sleep increased both sleep duration and academic performance. The intervention group received personalized bedtime reminders, morning feedback, and small cash rewards for meeting a seven-hour sleep goal. During the intervention, students in the treatment group increased their sleep by 19 minutes per night, with a 26% increase in the share of nights meeting the 7-hour goal. The effects on academic performance were significant, with an improvement of 0.075–0.089 grade points during the intervention semester. These effects persisted into the following semester, although the sleep duration effect diminished to 8 extra minutes per night after the incentives ended. The study also found that the benefits were strongest for freshmen and STEM students. The research was corroborated by multiple sources, including ScienceAlert, the National Bureau of Economic Research, and Phys.org.",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.sciencealert.com/a-simple-change-to-sleep-directly-boosts-academic-performance-study-reveals",
    "https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w32550/w32550.pdf",
    "https://www.nber.org/papers/w32550",
    "https://www.newswise.com/articles/incentives-to-sleep-boost-college-students-grades-new-study-finds"
  ],
